<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hudson's Bay Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1670</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hudson's Bay Company was chartered by Charles II in 1670 with a monopoly of trade in all lands draining into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-bay">Hudson Bay</a>, a territory called Rupert's Land. It ran the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cree">Cree</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assiniboine">Assiniboine</a> and other peoples from posts on the bay and later across the west, merging with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-company">North West Company</a> in 1821. It sold Rupert's Land to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> in 1870.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company.jpg" alt="Hudson's Bay Company" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hudson%27s_Bay_Company_Official_Logo_2013.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
